From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:25:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] perf(text): reuse generated pattern rectangles between
 frames

PatternSpecialDrawable allocated two lists and one GlyphRenderer.Rectangle
per piece (plus shadow and outline pieces) on every frame. Rectangles are
immutable and only read by GlyphRenderer.drawRectangle, so keep the lists
generated by the unchanged code in a weak identity map keyed by the
drawable, and regenerate them whenever any input (text color, outline
type and color, shadow flag, x or y) differs from the one they were built
with. The render layer and glyph renderer are still looked up per frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
